Grouping four CONTIGUOUS elements per thread changes intra-row summation order
away from the strided order, and the strided order is what produced the 5.3x
accuracy gain.  Speed and this accuracy gain are in direct tension: the scale
hoist requires contiguity, contiguity costs the accuracy.
